      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test file has:\n1. 14 unused data provider methods that belong to other tests\n2. Many unused imports\n\nI'll create a clean version that keeps only what's needed for this specific test.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored file removes all 14 unused data provider methods and trims imports down to only those actually needed, leaving a focused, self-explanatory test class that clearly conveys its single purpose: verifying that non-`IsoEra` instances are rejected by `Symmetry454Chronology.prolepticYear()` with a `ClassCastException`."
